# Compiling

Build both layouts from `paper/`:

```bash
cd paper
latexmk -pdf
```

`latexmkrc` lists `submit.tex` and `preprint.tex`, so a bare `latexmk -pdf` builds `submit.pdf` and `preprint.pdf`. To build only one, name it: `latexmk -pdf preprint.tex`.

MiKTeX's `latexmk` needs Perl. Without it, run the cycle by hand for each wrapper:

```bash
pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode preprint
bibtex preprint
pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode preprint
pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode preprint
```

`python util/build.py` does whichever of the two works and reports the problems below.

## A clean build

A change is not finished until both layouts compile with:

- zero errors;
- zero undefined references and zero undefined citations;
- no "multiply defined" labels;
- no overfull boxes wider than 1 pt in the body text (fix by rewording, not by `\sloppy`);
- no "Float too large" warnings.

`util/build.py` prints each of these from the logs and exits nonzero on any error, undefined reference or undefined citation.

Never commit build products (`*.aux`, `*.log`, `*.bbl`, the PDFs of `main`, `submit` and `preprint`); `paper/.gitignore` lists them.
